column5:
[NAME] Descriptive name. Eases a walker's pitch (+0x6c) toward the floor slope along its heading (+0x298). Sources: analysis ai-animation-runtime.md entities 2026-09-26; blind review (medium, as ENT_UpdatePitch); adjudicated PARTIAL. Facts (tools/check_names.py): const:298; const:7ff; const:fff; caller:ENT_TickEntity.

[DOCS_SYNC]
[docs/ai-animation-runtime.md > Update order] 1. swimming update; heading, bank and pitch += their rates (`+0x60/+0x68/+0x70`), then the yaw rate **halves** and the others lose ¼ each frame, and rates below a Δt-scaled floor snap to 0; walkers' pitch follows the floor slope (`ENT_TiltToSlope` (`0x4079f3`)); bank and pitch relax toward level (1/16 per frame while walking, ¼ otherwise);

[NAME] Descriptive name. Gives a free object a two-sided collision sphere of radius 50 at its node. Sources: analysis engine.md physics 2026-09-26; blind review (medium); adjudicated AGREE. Facts (tools/check_names.py): call:0045f490; call:0040bd2b; const:32; call:MDL_GetNodePosition.

[DOCS_SYNC]
[docs/engine.md > Colliders and radii] - **free objects** (`+0xa9 & 8`): `PHYS_AttachObjectCollider` (`0x40be46`), radius **50**, mass 10;

